ts, Cowork tasks or Code sessions, the app copies them into the user's first-party profile on the same computer; once the user resumes a copied session it behaves like any other first-party session. The copy also uploads the skills the user saved in that third-party configuration (under this organization or none) to their own skills in the organization, only where the organization lets members create skills and scans uploaded skills; otherwise nothing is uploaded. A skill whose SKILL.md declares hooks or tool permissions, or whose folder holds plugin files, is never uploaded. Where that configuration has local MCP servers, the app shows one notification offering to review them in Settings \u203A Import; no server is added without the user's confirmation there. If Anthropic has enabled memory import, that configuration's Cowork memory notes come too, unless the user had paused memory: used at once without review, never overwriting a note, synced like other Cowork memory. Chats, tasks and sessions themselves are not uploaded. The copy runs in the background, once per account and organization, and leaves the originals in place. Without this key, the organization's own setting (Admin settings in claude.ai) decides, and a deployed key takes precedence over it. A value that is not a UUID is reported as a configuration error and copies nothing; one that names a different organization than the one signed in copies nothing and is noted in the app's log. Like other first-party keys, deploying it puts the app's configuration under management, so a third-party connection a user set up in the app's own settings no longer applies. Anthropic can switch the copy off remotely.")},placeholder:yt.msg({defaultMessage:"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",id:"oT3AdLMVZK"})}),disableDeepLinks:pt.field(Tn.z.boolean().optional(),{flatKey:"disableDeepLinkRegistration",support:{enabled:{scopes:["3p"],availableInVersion:"1.6889.0"}},failClosedValue:!0,title:yt.msg({defaultMessage:"Disable claude:// deep-link handling",id:"CCUxBOb3va"}),default:!1,category:"sandbox",group:Pa.GENERAL_RESTRICTIONS_GROUP,order:9,description:{short:pt.shortDescription(yt.msg({defaultMessage:"Stop external apps and websites from opening Claude Desktop via claude:// links.",id:"0I38l/TM7C"}))}}),disableConnectorSignInInApp:pt.field(Tn.z.boolean().optional(),{flatKey:"disableConnectorSignInInApp",support:{enabled:{scopes:["1p"],availableInVersion:"2.26454.0"},visibility:"public-undocumented"},failClosedValue:!0,appBehaviorOnly:!0,title:yt.msg({defaultMessage:"Keep connector sign-in in the browser",id:"QjCp+5pd3a"}),default:!1,category:"connectors",description:{short:pt.shortDescription(yt.msg({defaultMessage:"Finish claude.ai connector (MCP) sign-ins in the browser rather than letting the app finish them from a claude:// link.",id:"hPVthk75/t"})),long:pt.longDescription("When true, a claude.ai connector's (remote MCP server's) OAuth sign-in started from Claude Desktop runs and completes in the system browser, and the claude:// link that then reopens the app only reports the outcome. When false (the default), on accounts where finishing in the app is available (a server-side rollout, not a setting in this configuration), the browser opens only the connector's own sign-in page and the app finishes the sign-in itself. Other claude:// links (chats, projects, Claude Code sessions) are unaffected; in third-party deployments `disableDeepLinkRegistration` turns those off. Set it through device management (MDM or machine policy); it applies from the app's next launch, and a value that cannot be read as true or false counts as true. An app-behavior key like `disableAutoUpdates`: a profile that sets any of them becomes the only source for all of them, so deploy them together; a profile that sets only such keys leaves the rest of the user's configuration in effect.")}}),microsoftAuthBroker:pt.field(Tn.z.enum(["auto","disabled","required"]).optional(),{flatKey:"microsoftAuthBroker",support